{
  "version": 1,
  "calibration": "Shares are sized for a 1M-token model (thread budget ~860K): tool_result 0.02 = ~17K tokens per result, read_page 0.04 = ~34K tokens per page, web_fetch 0.08 = ~69K tokens of page text kept for paging, grep_line 0.0005 = ~430 tokens per matching line. Smaller windows scale down, larger up; nothing is capped.",
  "description": "Layered context budget. Every node takes `share` of its parent's budget, floored at `min_tokens`; there are no ceilings. A node's children are only constrained once the node itself outgrows its allotment. Level 2 blocks keep their tags in the prompt; level 3 and deeper markers only partition the budget and are removed from what the model receives. Source of truth for laintas_cli/context_policy/budget.json, which is this file with every `hidden` node's children removed. Edit here and re-sync.",
  "hysteresis": 0.9,
  "assumed_window": 64000,
  "assumed_summary_window": 32768,
  "chars_per_token": 3.5,
